<title>USA: Platte River to shut Colo. coal unit for repair.</title>
<headline>Platte River to shut Colo. coal unit for repair.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Platte River Power Authority plans to shut its 262 megawatt Rawhide coal-fired power unit in northern Colorado for 24 hours beginning September 14 for repairs, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The unit, located about 20 miles north of Fort Collins, Colo., should restart, and resume full power production on September 15 following scheduled repairs on the unit's mainstream drain valves, spokesman Roy Rohla said Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
